


GETARG(3F)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           GETARG(3F)



NAME
     getarg, iargc - command arguments to Fortran

SYNOPSIS
     subroutine getarg( argno, string )
     integer argno
     character *(*) string

     iargc()

DESCRIPTION
     These procedures permit Fortran programs to access the com-
     mand arguments.  The integer function iargc returns the
     number of command arguments.  The subroutine getarg stores
     the nth command argument in its second argument.  The string
     is truncated or padded with blanks, in accord with the rules
     of Fortran character assignment.

     The command
            go arg1 argument2
     will return 2 as the value of iargc. If s is declared char-
     acter*4, then
           call getarg(2, s)
     will put "argu" in s.

SEE ALSO
     exec(2)




























